From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xorbidden <xorbidden@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:23:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] framebuffer: bind the panel's threads to chosen cores
 (fb_cores)

Boot-arg fb_cores=MASK binds the presenter to the first core of MASK
and helper i to the (i+2)-th, by cpu-id. The default, 0, leaves them to
the scheduler as before.

On davinci (two big cores, six small) the scaling at fb_pri took both
big cores for 4 to 7 ms of every frame, and the window server, put off
onto the small cores, drew there in 13.2 ms instead of 7.4 (rc.jobs.fps
with touch_lat=1, 2 November: 36% of frame steps over 16.7 ms).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
