 Made by `tools/boot-args.py --markdown`; CI fails if it is out of date with the source (`tools/boot-args.py --check`).
 
-Every argument that the kernel, the loader or user space of this port reads, and which file reads it. **343 arguments**: 280 read by the kernel, 14 by the loader, 59 by user space (one is read in more than one place).
+Every argument that the kernel, the loader or user space of this port reads, and which file reads it. **344 arguments**: 281 read by the kernel, 14 by the loader, 59 by user space (one is read in more than one place).
 
 This is a catalogue of what exists and who reads it, not a manual. What an argument means is in the head of the file that reads it. The stable switches have a symbol in the configuration (`tools/hakios-config.py help SYMBOL`, `docs/configs.md`); the rest are the knobs of bring-up (a driver's steps, pauses, traces, test modes) and can change with the driver. Any of them can be given in a configuration with `CONFIG_BOOTARGS="name=value ..."`, which checks that each name is in this list.
 
 Layers: **K** the kernel, **L** the loader, **U** user space (through `sysctl kern.bootargs`).
 
-## GPU and display (75)
+## GPU and display (76)
 
 | Argument | Layer | Read by | Configuration | Set by |
 |---|---|---|---|---|
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ Layers: **K** the kernel, **L** the loader, **U** user space (through `sysctl ke
 | `display_probe` | K | `hakios.adreno.c` | `CONFIG_DISPLAY_PROBE` |  |
 | `fb_beat` | K | `MiniIOMobileFramebuffer.cpp` | `CONFIG_FB_BEAT` |  |
